WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.235
CI/CD is where npm security practices
become repeatable.

2
00:00:06.315 --> 00:00:13.689
A strong pipeline uses npm ci, starts from
a clean environment, runs tests,

3
00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:20.675
reviews lockfile changes, performs
dependency and secret scanning,

4
00:00:20.755 --> 00:00:28.363
and fails on policy violations that the
team has agreed are release blockers.

5
00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:32.657
The goal is not to make every finding
fatal.

6
00:00:32.737 --> 00:00:39.643
The goal is to make dependency risk
visible, consistently evaluated,

7
00:00:39.723 --> 00:00:44.287
and handled before release pressure hides
it.

8
00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:48.464
Team workflow matters as much as tooling.

9
00:00:48.544 --> 00:00:53.694
Pull requests should make dependency
intent clear,

10
00:00:53.774 --> 00:00:59.978
especially when package.json or
package-lock.json changes.

11
00:01:00.058 --> 00:01:07.666
CODEOWNERS or required reviewers can route
dependency changes to people who

12
00:01:07.746 --> 00:01:09.852
understand the risk.

13
00:01:09.932 --> 00:01:14.029
Branch protections, release approvals,

14
00:01:14.109 --> 00:01:22.185
and documented exception processes help
prevent emergency habits from becoming

15
00:01:22.265 --> 00:01:23.436
permanent.

16
00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:28.549
When a dependency update is accepted
despite risk,

17
00:01:28.629 --> 00:01:33.779
the acceptance should have an owner and
review date.

18
00:01:33.859 --> 00:01:38.892
Secure npm workflows also reduce secret
exposure.

19
00:01:38.972 --> 00:01:47.282
Build jobs that install dependencies
should not automatically receive deployment

20
00:01:47.362 --> 00:01:48.182
tokens.

21
00:01:48.262 --> 00:01:54.348
Jobs that publish packages should be
isolated and protected.

22
00:01:54.428 --> 00:02:02.504
Cache usage should be deliberate so teams
do not preserve untrusted state between

23
00:02:02.584 --> 00:02:03.404
builds.

24
00:02:03.484 --> 00:02:09.219
When a pipeline is easy to rebuild from
source, lockfiles,

25
00:02:09.299 --> 00:02:17.960
and controlled registries, incident
response becomes more practical because the team

26
00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:22.020
can reproduce and inspect what shipped.
